{
  "about": "Source reads over a row's collected records and over ODM inputs (LOOKUP-8, COLUMN-2, NAME-9 to NAME-11). A filtered source, a mapping's source and a first_available's sources read their own row's collected records; a selected record without a value never takes an unselected record's value; a filtered read that keeps none of its row's records, also a row template's read of its own record, answers the declared absent value, counted (NAME-6), and a first_available source's declared absent is present, so no later source is read; a conflict counts the values its filter keeps; a filter cannot read another relation; equal dates are one value and distinct ones are counted; an ODM input reports its first record without a subject key and how many lack one; and a column odm read takes the ODM scope of the row template that built its row, also when an ODM input other than the base drives that template. An ODM XML input stores exactly the clinical-item table, and one an odm read reads exactly the eleven ODM fields as text (ODM-1, NAME-8), so check refuses a read of another field, arithmetic over the text Value and an ordinal naming a stored field as the run refuses them, from the declarations alone (#5077); each such case reads odm13.xml, whose items are I.DATE, I.EMPTY and I.NULL of SUBJECT-1. Moved from execution_retired_odm_context.rs, its retired_odm_context module. A test that saved is a save case with the bytes it compared, a test that read the run's issues compared them whole, and the handler counts one test compared whole are the report's handler rows at SPEC_PATH, NAME and COUNT. Every value is its test's.",
  "documents": {
    "odm_xml": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: DM\nkeys: [SUBJECT]\ninput: {ODM: {path: source.xml}}\noutput: {path: dm.csv, columns: [SUBJECT, X]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: SUBJECT, type: str, derivation: ODM.SubjectKey}\n  - {name: X, type: str, derivation: ODM.TYPO}\n",
    "odm_value": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: OUT\nkeys: [SubjectKey]\ninput: {ODM: odm.csv}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [SubjectKey, VALUE]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: SubjectKey, type: str, derivation: ODM.SubjectKey}\n  - {name: VALUE, type: str, derivation: ODM.Value}\n",
    "odm_target": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: OUT\nkeys: [GroupID]\ninput: {ODM: odm.csv}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [GroupID, VALUE]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: GroupID, type: str, derivation: ODM.GroupID}\n  - {name: VALUE, type: str, derivation: {source: {variable: ODM.Value, filter: \"ODM.RecordKind = 'TARGET'\"}}}\n",
    "odm_date": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: OUT\nkeys: [SubjectKey]\ninput: {ODM: {path: odm.csv, types: {VISITDT: date}}}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [SubjectKey, VALUE]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: SubjectKey, type: str, derivation: ODM.SubjectKey}\n  - {name: VALUE, type: date, derivation: ODM.VISITDT}\n",
    "odm_driver": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: OUT\nkeys: [ID, SEQ]\nbase: BASE\ninput: {BASE: base.csv, SRC: odm.csv}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [ID, SEQ, VAL]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str}\n  - {name: SEQ, type: int, derivation: {row_number: {window: {order_by: [ID]}}}}\n  - {name: VAL, type: str, derivation: {odm: SRC.IT.TEST.OID}}\nrows:\n  - id: occurrence\n    dataset: SRC\n    filter: \"SRC.ItemOID = 'IT.ANCHOR'\"\n    derivations: {ID: \"'one'\"}\n",
    "items": "StudyOID,SubjectKey,ItemOID,Value\nS1,001,IT.DM.SEX,Male\nS1,001,IT.DM.AGE,34\nS1,001,IT.DM.ARM,Placebo\n",
    "visit_dates": "StudyOID,SubjectKey,VISITDT,ItemOID,Value\nS1,001,2025-01-02,IT.A,a\nS1,001,2025-01-02,IT.B,b\n",
    "occurrences": "StudyOID,MetaDataVersionOID,SubjectKey,StudyEventOID,StudyEventRepeatKey,FormOID,FormRepeatKey,ItemGroupOID,ItemGroupRepeatKey,ItemOID,Value\nS,M,P,E,,F,,G,,IT.ANCHOR,anchor\nS,M,P,E,,F,,G,,IT.TEST.OID,Y\n"
  },
